Description: APPLICATION_DESCRIPTION
 Poet Music plays the music that is already on your disk. There is no account,
 no catalogue and no sign-in: you point it at a folder, it reads the tags,
 cover art and .lrc lyric files it finds there, and that is your library.
 .
 Browsing is by song, album, artist, genre or playlist, with live search and a
 sort order that is remembered between sessions. Now Playing carries a seek
 bar, synced lyrics, a ten-band equaliser, playback-speed steps and a sleep
 timer that can end on a clock or after a set number of songs.
 .
 The queue is a Musicolet-style working copy rather than an engine setting:
 shuffling writes a new fixed order around the song currently playing,
 un-shuffling puts the original order back, and "play next" inserts directly
 after the current track. The queue, position and modes survive a restart.
 .
 A built-in tag editor writes to MP3, FLAC, OGG and M4A — titles through to
 composer and comment, embedded artwork, unsynced lyrics, and a synced-LRC
 maker that stamps timestamps against live playback. The Listening Journal
 reports on your own archive: totals, top artists and albums, listening
 habits and library health, all counted locally.
 .
 Playback is the system's GStreamer, so it uses the codecs already installed,
 and the interface is a WebKitGTK view in a GTK window over a server bound to
 the loopback address only. Nothing is sent anywhere.
Depends: PACKAGE_DEFAULT_DEPENDENCIES PACKAGE_CUSTOM_DEPENDENCIES
